The provided class `DisposableAutoReleaseMultiObserver` is a thin wrapper around RxJava observer callbacks, primarily handling disposal state and delegating to user-provided `Consumer`/`Action` instances. Its logic is straightforward and does not contain computationally intensive or algorithmic code that would benefit from micro‑benchmarking. Benchmarking such a utility would mainly measure the overhead of the surrounding RxJava infrastructure rather than the class itself, making a dedicated JMH test unnecessary.